# The live cast of one player for the admin app (server/README.md "Live spectator", phase 2; docs/ADMIN_APP.md
# "Assistir jogador"). Owner, 2026-10-23: "Eu quero ver o gameplay em tempo real. Faça o patch na engine."
#   * castPort (config.lua, default 0 = off; castMaxSpectators 3, castQueueKb 1024): a TCP port on 127.0.0.1 only,
#     with its own thread (src/chaoscastserver.cpp). Game.setCastTarget(name) names the watched player ("" or nil
#     clears it; Game.getCastTarget() -> name, spectators, port open). remote_cmd.lua sets it for the line
#     "cast NAME" (chaos-ctl.sh cast NAME).
#   * ProtocolGame::writeToOutputBuffer, the one place every game message of a player goes through, also hands the
#     watched player's messages to the cast port. src/chaoscast.h keeps only the game view: map, tiles, creatures,
#     moves, effects, missiles, animated text, health, light, the player's stats, speech on screen (say, yell,
#     monster speech) and the damage / heal / experience numbers. Private and channel messages, the channel list,
#     VIP, modal windows, store, market, trade, containers, inventory, the outfit window, extended opcodes and pings
#     never leave the engine.
#   * A frame is u16 length + one message body, plain (no checksum, no XTEA). A new spectator gets a hello frame
#     (opcode 0x00: "CAST", version, player id, client marker, item / text flags, aware range, name), then the view
#     a login sends (aware range, map, stats, light; ProtocolGame::writeCastView, which starts the connection's
#     known creatures again so every creature in view goes out in full), then the live messages in order.
#   * The game thread never waits: a spectator more than castQueueKb behind is dropped; everyone is dropped when the
#     target changes, logs out or its connection is replaced (the relay connects again for a fresh view). At most
#     castMaxSpectators (1-8) at once; more connections are closed at once.
# server/tools/cast_relay.py reads the port and turns the frames into the app's JSON lines.
# New headers src/chaoscast.h (pure; tests in server/tools/chaoscast_test.cpp, CI) and src/chaoscastserver.h.
# Applies after 0001-0063.
